      "label": "Server-to-Server Login Pattern",
      "file_type": "rationale",
      "source_file": "plan/00-master-plan.md",
      "source_location": null,
      "source_url": null,
      "captured_at": null,
      "author": null,
      "contributor": null,
      "rationale": "Upstream Set-Cookie: VB-AUTH=...; Domain=localhost can never be stored by a browser on a different domain, so login must happen server-to-server and spotdl-web mints its own session cookie rather than forwarding VB-AUTH to the browser.",
      "id": "plan_00_master_plan_auth_server_to_server_pattern",
      "community": 7,
      "norm_label": "server-to-server login pattern"
    },
    {
      "label": "Email Allowlist Authorization Gate",
      "file_type": "rationale",
      "source_file": "plan/00-master-plan.md",
      "source_location": null,
      "source_url": null,
      "captured_at": null,
      "author": null,
      "contributor": null,
      "rationale": "POST /auth/register is public on vb2007.hu-api, so a successful upstream login only proves the account is real, not that the person may use spotdl-web; ALLOWED_EMAILS is the actual authorization gate, and rejection must be indistinguishable from a wrong password.",
